    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d50">

                <pb facs="0140" n="1598" xml:id="pg1598"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source"> NSC–S/S Files: Lot 63 D 351: NSC 101
                    Series</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Executive Secretary of the National
                        Security Council</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lay</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the National Security Council </hi><anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d50-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-03-21">March 21, 1951</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Memorandum for the National Security Council</hi>
                </p>
                <p rendition="#flush">Subject: United States Action to Counter Chinese Communist
                    Aggression</p>
                <table>
                    <row>
                        <cell>References: </cell>
                        <cell>A. NSC 101 Series<anchor n="2" xml:id="d50-f2"/>
                        </cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell/>
                        <cell>B. NSC Action No. 420-<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi><anchor n="3"
                                xml:id="d50-f3"/>
                        </cell>
                    </row>
                </table>
                <p>The enclosed study of the military effectiveness of the possible use of Chinese
                    forces on Formosa against the mainland of China, submitted by the Joint Chiefs
                    of Staff in response to the reference action, is transmitted herewith at the
                    request of the Secretary of Defense for the information of the National Security
                    Council. It is also being referred to the Senior NSC Staff for use in connection
                    with the current project on “United States National Objectives and Policy in
                        Asia”.<anchor n="4" xml:id="d50-f4"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">James</hi> S. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lay,
                            Jr.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d50-a1.xml" xpointer="d50-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d50-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d50-f1-content">
                <p>A handwritten notation on the source text indicated that it was seen by Secretary
                    Acheson.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d50-f2" n="2" xml:id="d50-f2-content">
                <p>The texts of NSC 101, January 12, 1951, and NSC 101/1, January 15, 1951, may be
                    found on <ref target="frus1951v07p1#pg_70">pp. 70</ref> and <ref
                        target="frus1951v07p1#pg_79">79</ref>; for text of the State Department
                    draft of NSC 101/1, January 17, 1951, see <ref target="#pg1515">p.
                    1515</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d50-f3" n="3" xml:id="d50-f3-content">
                <p> NSC Action No. 420-<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>, taken at the NSC meeting on
                    January 17, 1951, requested the Joint Chiefs of Staff to prepare “a detailed
                    study of the military effectiveness of the possible use of Chinese forces on
                    Formosa against the mainland of China, including consideration of the effect of
                    such use upon the defense of Formosa.” (NSC–S/S Miscellaneous Files: Lot 66 D
                    95).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d50-f4" n="4" xml:id="d50-f4-content">
                <p>The project culminated with the approval of NSC 48/5 on May 17, 1951; see the
                    editorial note, <ref target="#pg1671">p. 1671</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
